  ],
  "script": "Beta seven just landed. The one that decides what actually ships to your phone next month. It dropped August 24th, one week after beta six. And there's a pattern in what's actually inside. No new features this week. Just Apple finishing what it already announced. Because beta seven's release notes read like a fix list, not a feature list. Take the alarm bug: you couldn't stop a ringing alarm without unlocking your phone. Fixed. Or Portrait mode, where the blur was rendering wrong on photos. Also fixed. Even the new Siri voice, which was reverting to the old one whenever your phone overheated \u2014 patched. And dictation's running on a more accurate on-device model \u2014 there's a toggle waiting in Keyboard settings. None of that is exciting. That's exactly the point. Seven betas in, Apple isn't adding features anymore. It's closing out what would've shipped broken in September. Every outlet watching this cycle says the same thing \u2014 no new features, just stability, weeks from release. So the number that matters here was never the features. It's the seven. Because that's the number deciding what ships. One more beta, maybe two. Then the RC. Then it's just... iOS 27.",
